  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#mapping_001",
  "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
  "instance_name": "mapping_001",
  "label": "The audience's exaggerated shock is mapped onto the concept of a 'stupid post'",
  "description": "The text 'y'all wanna see a stupid post' is juxtaposed with the visual of an audience reacting with extreme shock and awe. This creates an analogical mapping where the intense, dramatic reaction of the audience (visual material) is being humorously equated to the anticipated reaction to a trivial or silly post (textual material). The mapping is based on the contrast: the visual shows a reaction that is disproportionate to the mundane content implied by the text, creating a comedic effect. The 'stupid post' is the entity being mapped onto the visual reaction.",
